    questionText: "The Stieltjes integrals satisfy \\( G(x)=\\frac{d}{dx}\\big[x\\,F(x)\\big] \\), with series \\( F\\sim\\sum(-1)^n n!\\,x^n \\) and \\( G\\sim\\sum(-1)^n(n+1)!\\,x^n \\). Show that the least-term index of \\( G \\) is one less than that of \\( F \\) for the same \\( x \\), and explain why this differentiation shifts the optimal truncation point.",
