    questionText: "Consider \\( I(x)=\\displaystyle\\int_0^\\infty \\frac{e^{-t}}{1+x^2 t}\\,dt \\). Find its asymptotic series in powers of \\( x^2 \\), locate the least term at \\( x = 0.4 \\) (so \\( x^2 = 0.16 \\)), and use optimal truncation to estimate \\( I(0.4) \\). (Reference value \\( I(0.4)=0.875687 \\).)",
